wo, leaves a Gibbs measure of finite range whose Dobrushin row sum is at most 0.9963, with constants proved from Turán's inequality for the modified Bessel functions (Lemma 8.6); the infinite-volume Gibbs measure is therefore unique, correlations of local observables decay exponentially, and the transfer matrix has a mass gap. The numbers of its certificate are evaluated on three roads that share no line, and with the exact constants, enclosed in a gate run of record, the bound extends to β ≤ 0.2452; the derivation's test from outside, a search from below over the decimated specification, found no configuration exceeding its constants, and a second reader's independent line-by-line read found no defect. The theorem is a statement about the lattice theory at strong coupling; it reaches no crossover and proves nothing about the continuum limit, where the four-dimensional mass gap remains open. The paper closes Section 8.3 by stating the open part exactly: the group enters only through the evaluation of Hypothesis I, the weak end has no published coupling (Bałaban's four-dimensional stability is proved under the hypothesis that every effective coupling of the sequence stays below a constant; the discharge of that hypothesis, his Theorem 2, was announced in 1987 and never published, and it is a theorem on this work's path, stated exactly on the open ledger with its falsifier), the distance is [0.2452, 1/γ²] with γ unread, and the tools that would cross it are named and not claimed. Section 6.6 places six further claims in public view beside the corpus: the OpenAI announcement of 26 October 2026, the published paper of Faizal and Shabir, read at the five places where its argument must carry weight, the Zenodo manuscripts of Fontes (its one-block constants re-derived on three roads: its Hessian a truncation, its entropy bound failing at four plaquettes, its Peierls condition failing at its own parameters by a factor 2.24) and of Lee, a GitHub repository announcing a resolution for SU(3), and a Zenodo record proving a strong-coupling Hamiltonian gap that claims no crossing, each read at the page where its gap is obtained; Section 8 carries, of record, the sharp one-link constant 2β/(3π) with the disks 3π/72 and 3π/56, the certified hierarchical descent and the transform on an exact tube, and states why the block criterion's widening is not yet a theorem.
 
