nk, with no inequality yet that sees the cancellation), and reads θ ≤ 2^{(m−1)/k} on the dense vertices it would need (1.5 at k = 12, below the divergence line's 1.63), useless below k = 9. So the full gas has no proved number tonight: its rate is 3θ(s)⁴ with θ(s) known exactly for small s, and the tail is the lemma above or the complete sweep, whichever lands first; the sub-gas number 0.4709/0.4759 stands as the proved reach of the singly-attached class. Nothing above β = 0.2452 is claimed.
